WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.719
A single paper user token splits into two.

00:00:03.719 --> 00:00:09.089
Two become four, and four become eight.
The pattern feels simple, but its size

00:00:09.089 --> 00:00:09.856
changes quickly.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.652
Another row grows by adding the same
number each time.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:24.455
At first the rows match, then repeated
multiplication pulls one row farther

00:00:24.455 --> 00:00:24.856
ahead.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:35.543
Now growth is twenty percent per week. The
new users depend on the group

00:00:35.543 --> 00:00:38.689
already present, so each week adds a
different number.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.665
A target of two hundred appears above the
path.

00:00:48.665 --> 00:00:53.354
Counting one week at a time works, but the
crossing may happen between weekly

00:00:53.354 --> 00:00:53.689
reports.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:04.779
The time hides inside an exponent. We know
the starting group, the multiplier,

00:01:04.779 --> 00:01:08.272
and the target, but we need an operation
that uncovers time.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:19.688
When will this model reach the target?
Find the continuous crossing time, then

00:01:19.688 --> 00:01:23.106
decide which whole-week report first shows
the target has been reached.
